    "intro": "Selling mugs at markets, opening a clay studio or running pottery painting parties? This **pottery business name generator** has ceramics names in seven styles, ready to check before you stamp your pots.",
    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check a pottery business name is free?",
        "answer": "Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name to see whether it is free as a company name, a web address and a social media handle. In the UK, search the Companies House register; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Do this before you pay for a logo, labels or signage."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should a pottery business name say pottery or ceramics?",
        "answer": "<em>Pottery</em> sounds warm and handmade and suits a studio, a shop or classes; <em>Ceramics</em> sounds more design-led and suits a tableware brand or a gallery maker; <em>Clay Co.</em> sits between the two. If you mostly sell online, a short name without either word (such as <em>Kaolin</em>) is easier to fit on a maker's stamp and a handle."
      }
    ]
